# SOC2 audit engagement phase 1: Scoping & System Description — Solace
# Cloud case study (a fictional B2B SaaS company's first SOC2 Type II
# audit). One domain FRAGMENT of the shared solace-soc2-audit-cycle
# domain: this phase's 3 actions chain
# audit-engaged -> scoping-step1-done -> scoping-step2-done -> scoping-complete,
# so the merged cycle plan can only reach this phase after the problem's
# init atom is asserted. 8-constraint split: every precondition/effect/goal
# here is a 1-conjunct (and ...) — far inside PDDL8_MAX_CONJUNCTS=8 — and
# each action takes 1 parameter (PDDL8_MAX_PARAMS=8); soc2_test.rs asserts
# these bounds mechanically for every fragment (reusing
# crate::bench::togaf::verify_eight_constraint_split verbatim).
#
# COMPLIANCE-OVERCLAIM FENCE: no action effect below is named "compliant"
# or "opinion" — the audit ENGAGEMENT PROCESS is modeled here, never a
# compliance verdict. See packs/soc2-audit-pack/ontology.ttl for the full
# fence disclosure.
#
# Public-ontology doctrine: the artifact node is a blank node; the phase is
# identified by its public SKOS notation. The only private predicate is
# the cng pipeline's ABI carrier ceng:pddlDomain (urn:chatman:engine#),
# disclosed in packs/soc2-audit-pack/ontology.ttl.
@prefix ceng:    <urn:chatman:engine#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

_:artifact
    skos:notation "AUDIT-SCOPING" ;
    dcterms:description "Scoping & System Description domain fragment of the solace-soc2-audit-cycle STRIPS domain."@en ;
    ceng:pddlDomain """
(define (domain solace-soc2-audit-cycle)
  (:requirements :strips)
  (:predicates
    (audit-engaged ?x)
    (scoping-step1-done ?x)
    (scoping-step2-done ?x)
    (scoping-complete ?x))
  (:action define-system-boundary
    :parameters (?x)
    :precondition (and (audit-engaged ?x))
    :effect (and (scoping-step1-done ?x)))
  (:action select-in-scope-tsc-categories
    :parameters (?x)
    :precondition (and (scoping-step1-done ?x))
    :effect (and (scoping-step2-done ?x)))
  (:action document-system-description
    :parameters (?x)
    :precondition (and (scoping-step2-done ?x))
    :effect (and (scoping-complete ?x))))
""" .
